",{},"Direct construction"]],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Build one chosen improvement on suitable worked tiles as this hearth develops. Applying a commission can pay for its first order immediately. Further orders begin after each turn’s upkeep and production charters."],["LABEL",{},"Commission improvement",["SELECT",{"disabled":""},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"improvement.terraced_fields"},"Terraced fields"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.managed_woodlot"},"Managed woodlot"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.quarry"},"Measured quarry"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.reedworks"},"Reedworks"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.shore_fishery"},"Shore fishery"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.spring_garden"},"Spring garden"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.polder"},"Polder"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.grove_archive"},"Grove archive"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.oreworks"},"Oreworks"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.tide_observatory"},"Tide observatory"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.grange"},"Hearthgrain grange"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.iron_mine"},"Ironstone mine"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.copper_mine"},"Copper mine"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.salt_house"},"Salt house"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.timber_yard"},"Heartwood yard"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.remount_yard"},"Remount yard"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.silver_mine"},"Silver mine"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.glass_refinery"},"Ashglass refinery"]]],["DIV",{"class":"land-policy-amounts"},["LABEL",{},"Remaining allowance · coin",["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"100","inputmode":"numeric","disabled":"","aria-invalid":"false","type":"text","value":"100"}]],["LABEL",{},"Treasury reserve · coin",["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"40","inputmode":"numeric","disabled":"","aria-invalid":"false","type":"text","value":"40"}]]],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Applying replaces the remaining allowance with this amount; it does not add to it. Zero allowance stops new purchases. Terrain, research, the reserve and ordinary construction prices still apply."],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","class":"primary wide","disabled":""},"Apply land commission"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"The allowance limits total future spending; it is not taken from the treasury in advance. Each order must leave the chosen treasury reserve. Other realm orders can still spend that reserve. Commissions share the treasury in stable hearth order."],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Only unimproved, worked land is considered. A resource deposit accepts only its matching extraction site. Existing sites are kept; commissions do not claim land, cultivate biomes or assign workers."],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Siege and occupation pause work. Ending a commission keeps paid work underway. Building, cultivating or cancelling land work yourself ends the commission after a successful order. Losing the hearth ends it; cancelled work is not refunded."]],["DETAILS",{"class":"land-options","data-testid":"settlement-road"},["SUMMARY",{},"Road connections"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Settlements gradually connect to an older town along a charted land route. Workers survey one town per realm each turn. Completed roads cross forest and hills for 1 movement point and remain after conquest."],["P",{},"Explore toward another owned settlement to establish a connection. Water and mountains require another route."]],["P",{"class":"land-stage","data-testid":"settlement-stage"},"colony"," · Capital"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Colony: 1–2 people · Settlement: 3–7 · City: 8+. Capital is a separate designation."],["P",{"data-testid":"land-counts"},"7"," claimed tiles · ","0"," / ","1"," assigned workers · reach ","2"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Connected territory and population can keep growing. Each person can work one additional tile. Larger hearths need more food, investment and civic upkeep."],["P",{"class":"field-help","data-testid":"hearth-growth-economy"},"Next person: ","0"," / ","12"," food · consumption ","2"," food per turn · civic upkeep ","1"," coin (","1"," population, ","0"," territory, ","0"," administration)."],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Realm coin per turn: ","7"," income − ","2"," upkeep = ","5",". Queued formations add ","0"," upkeep when completed."],["SECTION",{"class":"border-growth","aria-label":"Border growth","data-testid":"border-growth"},["P",{},["STRONG",{},"Border growth:"]," ","0"," / ","8"," civic progress · +","1"," per active turn"],["PROGRESS",{"aria-label":"Civic progress toward next border","value":"0","max":"8"}],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Next expansion: hex ","625",". About ","8"," active turns at this rate. Larger populations, markets, archives and Surveyed estates support growth."],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Expansion claims one connected, charted tile at a time. It does not build improvements. Workers remain under manual control unless you choose a worker policy. Siege and occupation pause growth; conquest resets its progress. Buying a tile is immediate and increases the next expansion threshold."]],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"The center is worked for free. Borders do not block travel. Only worked tiles contribute their yields; natural features remain after cultivation."],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Map borders mark the realm perimeter. Select tiles to inspect this town’s individual claims. Dim land shows remembered ownership, not live i